IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`
IMPORT `je21-art02-making`

-- je21-art04-08-effects: Articles 4 to 8 of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 (L.8/2021):
-- 4 Exercise of statutory powers before commencement of Jersey legislation, 5 Effect of repeal and expiry,
-- 6 Effect of repeal and re-enactment of Jersey legislation, 7 Amendment of Jersey subordinate legislation by a Law, etc,
-- 8 Power to amend Law consequential on another Law lodged but not made before its registration.
--
-- A function whose name says "permits", "applies" or "is not barred" answers whether the Article gives that effect.
-- FALSE then means the Article does not give it; it does not mean the Law forbids it, and the seat module (je21-seat.l4) says so when it asks.
-- A phrase "unless provision is made to the contrary" is an input: the caller says whether a contrary provision exists, and the Law is not asked to guess.
--
-- Forks registered here: L5 (what legislation "made by the States" is, from Article 2), L9 (Article 5 and legislation that expires), L10 (Article 5(3) where a contrary provision displaces Article 5(2)).

§ `Article 4 -- Exercise of statutory powers before commencement of Jersey legislation`

§§ `4(1) The powers the Article covers`

-- Answers: does Article 4 cover this power?
-- It covers a power conferred by Jersey legislation to do any of the things in (a) to (f); (f), "any other thing for the purposes of the legislation", leaves out only a power that is none of these.
-- src:56 | (1) This Article applies to any Jersey legislation that confers power to –
-- src:57 | (a) make any Jersey subordinate legislation;
-- src:58 | (b) establish an entity;
-- src:59 | (c) make an appointment;
-- src:60 | (d) give a notice or document;
-- src:61 | (e) prescribe a form; or
-- src:62 | (f) do any other thing for the purposes of the legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 4(1) (src:56-62)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of power in Article 4(1)`
      `the legislation conferring the power is Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 4(1): Article 4 applies to the power` kind `the legislation conferring the power is Jersey legislation` MEANS
    `the legislation conferring the power is Jersey legislation`
    AND CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a power to establish an entity` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a power to make an appointment` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a power to give a notice or document` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a power to prescribe a form` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a power to do any other thing for the purposes of the legislation` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a power of none of these kinds` THEN FALSE

§§ `4(2) Exercise after the making of the legislation, whether or not it is in force`

-- Answers: does Article 4(2) permit the power to be exercised now?
-- It does, at any time after the making of the legislation, "whether or not the legislation is in force", unless provision is made to the contrary (an input).
-- src:63 | (2) The power in question may, unless provision is made to the contrary, be exercised at any time after the making of the legislation, whether or not the legislation is in force.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 4(2) (src:63)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of power in Article 4(1)`
      `the legislation conferring the power is Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legislation conferring the power has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 4(2): Article 4 permits the power to be exercised before the legislation is in force` kind `the legislation conferring the power is Jersey legislation` `the legislation conferring the power has been made` `provision is made to the contrary` MEANS
        `Article 4(1): Article 4 applies to the power` kind `the legislation conferring the power is Jersey legislation`
    AND `the legislation conferring the power has been made`
    AND NOT `provision is made to the contrary`

§§ `4(3) Subordinate legislation made under the power is not brought into force before the power comes into force`

-- Answers: is bringing the subordinate legislation into force on this day barred by Article 4(3)?
-- Barred only if the day is before the day the provision conferring the power comes into force.
-- On the same day it is not before, taken at the level of the day: both are in force from the day's beginning unless a time is stated, and the caller who has a time to compare uses Article 3's moments.
-- TRUE here means Article 4(3) does not bar it; it does not say that nothing else does.
-- src:64 | (3) However, no Jersey subordinate legislation made under this power may be brought into force before the provision conferring the power comes into force.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 4(3) (src:64)
GIVEN `the day the subordinate legislation is to come into force` IS A DATE
      `the day the provision conferring the power comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 4(3): bringing the subordinate legislation into force on that day is not barred` `the day the subordinate legislation is to come into force` `the day the provision conferring the power comes into force` MEANS
    `the day the subordinate legislation is to come into force` AT LEAST `the day the provision conferring the power comes into force`

§ `Article 5 -- Effect of repeal and expiry`

§§ `5(1) and 5(5) When Article 5 applies`

-- Answers: does Article 5 apply to this repeal or expiry?
-- It applies where Jersey legislation repeals other Jersey legislation or a provision of it (5(1)), and "repealed" includes having expired or otherwise ceased to have effect (5(5)).
-- Fork L9: whether legislation that expires with no repealing legislation is within paragraph (1).
-- src:66 | (1) This Article applies where any Jersey legislation repeals any other Jersey legislation or a provision of that legislation.
-- src:79 | (5) In this Article a reference to legislation being repealed includes a reference to its having expired or otherwise ceasing to have effect.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 5(1) and (5) (src:66, src:79)
GIVEN `the repealing instrument is Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what ended is Jersey legislation or a provision of Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      ended IS A `How legislation ended`
      reading IS A `Reading L9 of Article 5 and legislation that expires`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 5(1) and (5): Article 5 applies to the repeal or expiry` `the repealing instrument is Jersey legislation` `what ended is Jersey legislation or a provision of Jersey legislation` ended reading MEANS
    `what ended is Jersey legislation or a provision of Jersey legislation`
    AND CONSIDER ended
        WHEN `it was repealed` THEN `the repealing instrument is Jersey legislation`
        WHEN `it expired`
            THEN CONSIDER reading
                WHEN `Article 5 applies to legislation that has expired or otherwise ceased to have effect, whether or not other legislation repealed it` THEN TRUE
                WHEN `Article 5 applies only where Jersey legislation repeals other Jersey legislation` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `it otherwise ceased to have effect`
            THEN CONSIDER reading
                WHEN `Article 5 applies to legislation that has expired or otherwise ceased to have effect, whether or not other legislation repealed it` THEN TRUE
                WHEN `Article 5 applies only where Jersey legislation repeals other Jersey legislation` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `it has not ended` THEN FALSE

§§ `5(2) What a repeal does not affect`

-- Answers: does Article 5(2) preserve this thing from the repeal?
-- Each of (a) to (f) is preserved "unless provision is made to the contrary" (an input), when Article 5 applies.
-- src:67 | (2) Unless provision is made to the contrary, the repeal does not affect any of the following –
-- src:68 | (a) the validity, invalidity, effect or consequences of anything done or suffered under the repealed legislation (including any saving, transitional or validating provision);
-- src:69 | (b) any existing right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under that legislation;
-- src:70 | (c) any amendment of legislation made by the repealed legislation;
-- src:71 | (d) the previous operation of the repealed legislation or anything done or permitted under that legislation;
-- src:72 | (e) any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy that relates to anything set out in sub-paragraph (b);
-- src:73 | (f) any penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of any offence committed before the repeal of the legislation or breach of it that occurred before its repeal.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 5(2) (src:67-73)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing a repeal might affect`
      `Article 5 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 5(2): the repeal does not affect the thing` thing `Article 5 applies` `provision is made to the contrary` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `the validity, invalidity, effect or consequences of anything done or suffered under the repealed legislation`
        THEN `Article 5 applies` AND NOT `provision is made to the contrary`
    WHEN `an existing right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it`
        THEN `Article 5 applies` AND NOT `provision is made to the contrary`
    WHEN `an amendment of legislation made by the repealed legislation`
        THEN `Article 5 applies` AND NOT `provision is made to the contrary`
    WHEN `the previous operation of the repealed legislation, or anything done or permitted under it`
        THEN `Article 5 applies` AND NOT `provision is made to the contrary`
    WHEN `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy that relates to a right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability under it`
        THEN `Article 5 applies` AND NOT `provision is made to the contrary`
    WHEN `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred for an offence committed, or a breach, before the repeal`
        THEN `Article 5 applies` AND NOT `provision is made to the contrary`

§§ `5(3) Proceedings and penalties continue as if the legislation had not been repealed`

-- Answers: may the investigation, proceeding or remedy relating to an existing right be instituted, continued or enforced, or the penalty, forfeiture or punishment imposed, as if the legislation had not been repealed?
-- Paragraph (3) has no "unless" limb of its own.
-- Fork L10: on the reading taken, a contrary provision that displaces paragraph (2) displaces paragraph (3), which speaks only of things "mentioned in paragraph (2)";
-- on the other, paragraph (3) applies whatever paragraph (2) is subject to.
-- src:74 | (3) Any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy mentioned in paragraph (2) that relates to an existing right may be instituted, continued or enforced, and any penalty, forfeiture or punishment mentioned in that paragraph may be imposed, as if the legislation had not been repealed.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 5(3) (src:74)
GIVEN `Article 5 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy relating to an existing right, or a penalty, forfeiture or punishment, mentioned in paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
      reading IS A `Reading L10 of Article 5(3) where provision is made to the contrary`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 5(3): the proceeding may be brought or the penalty imposed as if the legislation had not been repealed` `Article 5 applies` `it is an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy relating to an existing right, or a penalty, forfeiture or punishment, mentioned in paragraph (2)` `provision is made to the contrary` reading MEANS
        `Article 5 applies`
    AND `it is an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy relating to an existing right, or a penalty, forfeiture or punishment, mentioned in paragraph (2)`
    AND CONSIDER reading
        WHEN `a contrary provision that displaces paragraph (2) displaces paragraph (3) too, which speaks only of things mentioned in paragraph (2)` THEN NOT `provision is made to the contrary`
        WHEN `paragraph (3) has no "unless" limb and applies even where paragraph (2) is displaced` THEN TRUE

§§ `5(4) What a repeal does not revive`

-- Answers: does Article 5(4) stop the repeal reviving this thing?
-- "Unless provision is made to the contrary" (an input), the repeal does not revive legislation repealed, a rule of law that has been abolished, or any other thing not in force or existing when the repeal takes effect.
-- src:75 | (4) Unless provision is made to the contrary the repeal of any legislation does not revive –
-- src:76 | (a) any legislation repealed;
-- src:77 | (b) any rule of law that has been abolished; or
-- src:78 | (c) any other thing not in force or existing at the time at which the repeal takes effect.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 5(4) (src:75-78)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing a repeal might revive`
      `Article 5 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 5(4): the repeal does not revive the thing` thing `Article 5 applies` `provision is made to the contrary` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `legislation that was repealed` THEN `Article 5 applies` AND NOT `provision is made to the contrary`
    WHEN `a rule of law that had been abolished` THEN `Article 5 applies` AND NOT `provision is made to the contrary`
    WHEN `any other thing not in force or existing when the repeal takes effect` THEN `Article 5 applies` AND NOT `provision is made to the contrary`

§ `Article 6 -- Effect of repeal and re-enactment of Jersey legislation`

-- Answers: is a reference in other Jersey legislation to a provision that has been repealed and re-enacted construed as a reference to the re-enacted provision?
-- It is, when Jersey legislation (whenever made) repeals Jersey legislation and re-enacts the provision with or without modification, and the reference is in other Jersey legislation,
-- "unless provision is made to the contrary" (an input).
-- The Article speaks of references in other Jersey legislation only, so a reference in anything else (a contract, UK extended legislation) is outside it.
-- src:81 | If any Jersey legislation (whenever made) repeals any Jersey legislation and re-enacts any of its provisions, with or without modification, references in any other Jersey legislation to the provisions so repealed, unless provision is made to the contrary, are construed as references to the provisions so re-enacted.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 6 (src:81)
GIVEN `the repealing instrument is Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument repealed is Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the repealing instrument re-enacts the provision, with or without modification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference is in other Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 6: the reference to the repealed provision is construed as a reference to the re-enacted provision` `the repealing instrument is Jersey legislation` `the instrument repealed is Jersey legislation` `the repealing instrument re-enacts the provision, with or without modification` `the reference is in other Jersey legislation` `provision is made to the contrary` MEANS
        `the repealing instrument is Jersey legislation`
    AND `the instrument repealed is Jersey legislation`
    AND `the repealing instrument re-enacts the provision, with or without modification`
    AND `the reference is in other Jersey legislation`
    AND NOT `provision is made to the contrary`

§ `Article 7 -- Amendment of Jersey subordinate legislation by a Law, etc`

-- Answers: does Article 7 say that this amendment of Jersey subordinate legislation does not of itself limit its further amendment or repeal by other subordinate legislation?
-- 7(1): an amendment by a Law does not.
-- 7(2): where the subordinate legislation was not made by the States, "Law" in (1) includes Regulations.
-- Anything else (an amendment by an Order, or Regulations amending Regulations) is not mentioned, and the model refuses.
-- src:83 | (1) An amendment of Jersey subordinate legislation by a Law does not of itself limit any further amendment or repeal of that subordinate legislation by other subordinate legislation.
-- src:84 | (2) In the case of Jersey subordinate legislation not made by the States, the reference in paragraph (1) to a Law includes Regulations.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 7 (src:83-84)
GIVEN `the form of the subordinate legislation amended` IS A `Form of legislation`
      `the form of the legislation that amended it` IS A `Form of legislation`
      `the reading of legislation made by the States` IS A `Reading L5 of legislation made by the States`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 7: the amendment does not of itself limit further amendment or repeal by other subordinate legislation` `the form of the subordinate legislation amended` `the form of the legislation that amended it` `the reading of legislation made by the States` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the form of the subordinate legislation amended`
    WHEN `a Law` THEN REFUSE "Article 7 is about the amendment of Jersey subordinate legislation, and a Law is not subordinate legislation"
    WHEN `UK extended legislation` THEN REFUSE "Article 7 is about the amendment of Jersey subordinate legislation, and UK extended legislation is not Jersey subordinate legislation"
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the form of the legislation that amended it`
        WHEN `a Law` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Regulations`
            THEN IF `Article 2: the legislation was made by the States` `the form of the subordinate legislation amended` `the reading of legislation made by the States`
                 THEN REFUSE "Article 7 says nothing of an amendment by Regulations of subordinate legislation made by the States"
                 ELSE TRUE
        WHEN `Triennial Regulations`
            THEN IF `Article 2: the legislation was made by the States` `the form of the subordinate legislation amended` `the reading of legislation made by the States`
                 THEN REFUSE "Article 7 says nothing of an amendment by Regulations of subordinate legislation made by the States"
                 ELSE TRUE
        OTHERWISE REFUSE "Article 7 says nothing of an amendment by anything but a Law, or, for subordinate legislation not made by the States, Regulations"

§ `Article 8 -- Power to amend Law consequential on another Law lodged but not made before its registration`

§§ `8(2) The relevant period of a Law`

-- Answers: do the relevant periods of two Laws overlap to any extent?
-- "relevant period" means the period beginning on the day a Law was lodged and ending on the day it was made, so both of those days are inside the period.
-- Two periods overlap to any extent if they have a day in common: each begins no later than the other ends.
-- A Law made before the day it was lodged has no such period, and the model refuses.
-- src:86 | (1) The States may by Regulations make amendments to any Law incidental to, supplemental to, or consequential upon, the making of another Law if the relevant periods of those 2 Laws overlap to any extent.
-- src:88 | “lodged” means lodged in accordance with standing orders;
-- src:89 | “relevant period” means the period beginning on the day a Law was lodged and ending on the day it was made.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 8(1) and (2) (src:86, src:88-89)
GIVEN `the day the first Law was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the day the first Law was made` IS A DATE
      `the day the second Law was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the day the second Law was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 8(1) and (2): the relevant periods of the two Laws overlap to any extent` `the day the first Law was lodged` `the day the first Law was made` `the day the second Law was lodged` `the day the second Law was made` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day the first Law was made` LESS THAN `the day the first Law was lodged`
            THEN REFUSE "a Law made before it was lodged has no relevant period under Article 8(2)"
        IF `the day the second Law was made` LESS THAN `the day the second Law was lodged`
            THEN REFUSE "a Law made before it was lodged has no relevant period under Article 8(2)"
        OTHERWISE
                `the day the first Law was lodged` AT MOST `the day the second Law was made`
            AND `the day the second Law was lodged` AT MOST `the day the first Law was made`

§§ `8(1) The power to amend`

-- Answers: does Article 8(1) give the States the power to make Regulations amending a Law consequentially on the making of another Law?
-- It does if the relevant periods of the two Laws overlap to any extent.
-- FALSE means Article 8 does not give the power; any other source of power is outside this Law.
-- src:86 | (1) The States may by Regulations make amendments to any Law incidental to, supplemental to, or consequential upon, the making of another Law if the relevant periods of those 2 Laws overlap to any extent.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 8(1) (src:86)
GIVEN `the day the Law to be amended was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the day the Law to be amended was made` IS A DATE
      `the day the other Law was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the day the other Law was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 8(1): Article 8 gives the States power to amend the Law consequentially on the other Law` `the day the Law to be amended was lodged` `the day the Law to be amended was made` `the day the other Law was lodged` `the day the other Law was made` MEANS
    `Article 8(1) and (2): the relevant periods of the two Laws overlap to any extent` `the day the Law to be amended was lodged` `the day the Law to be amended was made` `the day the other Law was lodged` `the day the other Law was made`
